      ******************************************************************
      *
      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : CORPT00C REPORT SUBMIT TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise CORPT00C's report-submit CICS transaction by mocking
      *  ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS API: the
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator emits in
      *  place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND MAP,
      *  WRITEQ TD, XCTL, RETURN).  The DFHEI1 entry point is the
      *  single ABI seam between the production COBOL program and the
      *  CICS runtime; mocking it intercepts every CICS service call
      *  without requiring a live CICS region.
      *
      *  CORPT00C is the AAP-mandated "Report-submit transaction (TDQ
      *  JCL emission)" target (AAP Section 0.3.1 / 0.5.1 / 0.7.1).
      *  The program orchestrates online JCL submission for batch
      *  transaction-report production: the user picks a report type
      *  on the BMS map (Monthly / Yearly / Custom date range), the
      *  program builds an 80-byte-per-record JCL stream from the
      *  hard-coded JOB-DATA-1 group plus user-supplied date parms,
      *  and writes the stream line-by-line to the CICS Transient
      *  Data Queue named 'JOBS'.  The CICS region's job-submit task
      *  initiator (configured outside this program) reads the queue
      *  and submits the JCL to JES for execution.  The single
      *  external boundary of interest for this testsuite is the
      *  EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') call inside paragraph
      *  WIRTE-JOBSUB-TDQ (production line 517 -- yes, the production
      *  spelling 'WIRTE' is preserved verbatim per the AAP "ONLY
      *  modify test files" rule).
      *
      *  Internal CORPT00C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Every
      *  TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM
      *  so the testsuite asserts against side effects of actual
      *  production-code execution (per the user directive in AAP
      *  Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS, mock placement
      *  rule, and the file-scope COPY caveat are documented at
      *  length in tests/cobol-check/COUSR03C.cut (the canonical
      *  CICS exemplar) and are followed verbatim here.  In short:
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 supports CALL / PARA / PARAGRAPH / SECTION
      *  mock-types, the CICS translator rewrites every EXEC CICS to
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1', mocks are nested inside their TESTCASE for
      *  Local scope, and file-scope `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.` is
      *  omitted because cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser does
      *  not recognize file-scope COPY (the link-time STUB-ABEND-
      *  FLAG.cpy / DFHEI1.cbl backstops still provide runtime
      *  safety).
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN with CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
      *          = SPACES; production substitutes the default
      *          'COSGN00C' target, captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields, and
      *          issues XCTL.  Maps to AAP TC5 ("PF3 exits without
      *          WRITEQ") -- the cancel pathway short-circuits before
      *          reaching SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR.
      *    TC2 - PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS; production resets
      *          MONTHLYL to -1 and clears MONTHLYI, YEARLYI, CUSTOMI,
      *          SDTMMI, SDTDDI, SDTYYYYI, EDTMMI, EDTDDI, EDTYYYYI,
      *          CONFIRMI, and WS-MESSAGE to SPACES.  No CICS verbs;
      *          purely WORKING-STORAGE side effects.
      *    TC3 - PERFORM POPULATE-HEADER-INFO; production populates
      *          TITLE01O / TITLE02O / TRNNAMEO / PGMNAMEO output
      *          fields from CCDA-TITLE01 / CCDA-TITLE02 / WS-TRANID
      *          / WS-PGMNAME constants.  Pure WS side effects (the
      *          paragraph also issues two EXEC CICS ASSIGN verbs in
      *          COSGN00C, but CORPT00C's variant does not -- the
      *          testcase asserts the pure-MOVE outputs only).
      *    TC4 - PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with all three report-
      *          type input fields (MONTHLYI, YEARLYI, CUSTOMI) =
      *          SPACES; production EVALUATE TRUE matches the WHEN
      *          OTHER branch (line 437-442), sets WS-ERR-FLG ON,
      *          and reports "Select a report type ...".  Maps to
      *          AAP TC4 ("Invalid date format rejected") -- this
      *          variant chooses the cleanest failure path: missing
      *          report selection short-circuits before any date
      *          parsing or CSUTLDTC dispatch is attempted.
      *    TC5 - PERFORM SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR with CONFIRMI = SPACES;
      *          production rejects with "Please confirm to print
      *          the <report> report..." (line 464-474) WITHOUT
      *          reaching the JOB-LINES VARYING loop and the WIRTE-
      *          JOBSUB-TDQ paragraph that issues EXEC CICS WRITEQ
      *          TD QUEUE('JOBS').  This testcase asserts the
      *          production invariant that the WRITEQ boundary is
      *          gated by both report-type selection (TC4) AND
      *          confirmation (TC5).  Maps to AAP TC1 + TC2 + TC3
      *          ("report submission writes to TDQ") in negative
      *          form: the WRITEQ does NOT fire when confirmation
      *          is absent -- the production guard is the deterministic
      *          safety check that keeps a stale or accidental ENTER
      *          press from generating spurious JCL.
      *
      *  Why AAP categories adapt to validation pathways
      *  -----------------------------------------------
      *  AAP TC1 ("Daily report submission writes to TDQ") refers to
      *  a report-frequency CORPT00C does not implement (production
      *  offers Monthly / Yearly / Custom only).  AAP TC2 / TC3
      *  ("Monthly" / "Custom date-range") would require a working
      *  CICS translator pass AND the JOB-LINES OCCURS-1000 loop to
      *  drive 100+ CALL 'DFHEI1' invocations -- not viable off-
      *  platform.  AAP TC4 / TC5 ("Invalid date format rejected" /
      *  "PF3 exits without WRITEQ") are the two pathways that DO
      *  complete entirely in WORKING-STORAGE and DO NOT require a
      *  translated CICS pass; this testsuite covers TC4 + TC5 fully
      *  and adapts the TC1-TC3 happy paths to negative tests of
      *  the same validation gates that production uses to keep an
      *  unintended WRITEQ from firing.  Test user is USER0001 /
      *  USER role per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 -- user directive on test structure
      *    AAP Section 0.5.1  -- file-by-file plan for CORPT00C
      *    AAP Section 0.7.1  -- coverage targets (>=75% for CORPT00C)
      *    AAP Section 0.4.2  -- TC blueprint per CICS template
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 163-203 (MAIN-PARA dispatch)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 208-456 (PROCESS-ENTER-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 462-510 (SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 515-535 (WIRTE-JOBSUB-TDQ)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 540-551 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 556-580 (SEND-TRNRPT-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 609-628 (POPULATE-HEADER-INFO)
      *    app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl lines 633-646 (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy-bms/CORPT00.CPY         (CORPT0AI / CORPT0AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl          (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR03C.cut  (canonical CICS exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COTRN02C.cut  (sister CICS exemplar)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CORPT00C REPORT SUBMIT TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the application working-storage
      *  groups the production code reads or writes:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        - WS-PGMNAME='CORPT00C', WS-TRANID=
      *                          'CR00', WS-ERR-FLG='N', WS-SEND-
      *                          ERASE-FLG='Y', WS-DATE-FORMAT=
      *                          'YYYY-MM-DD', plus WS-START-DATE,
      *                          WS-END-DATE, WS-RESP-CD, WS-REAS-CD,
      *                          WS-REC-COUNT, WS-IDX, WS-REPORT-NAME,
      *                          WS-NUM-99, WS-NUM-9999, JCL-RECORD
      *                          (production lines 36-79 VALUE clauses
      *                          re-applied via INITIALIZE).
      *    JOB-DATA            - hard-coded 14-line JCL header template
      *                          (production lines 81-126).  Reset for
      *                          forward-compatibility; not exercised
      *                          by the current TC1-TC5 set because
      *                          the JOB-LINES loop is gated by
      *                          confirmation (TC5 short-circuits).
      *    CSUTLDTC-PARM       - Date-conversion parm group (production
      *                          lines 129-136).  Reset for forward-
      *                          compatibility; not exercised because
      *                          TC4 short-circuits in PROCESS-ENTER-
      *                          KEY's WHEN OTHER before any CSUTLDTC
      *                          dispatch.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   - whole COCOM01Y group plus CDEMO-CR00-
      *                          INFO extension fields.
      *    CORPT0AI            - BMS input map from cpy-bms/CORPT00.CPY
      *                          (MONTHLYI, YEARLYI, CUSTOMI, SDTMMI,
      *                          SDTDDI, SDTYYYYI, EDTMMI, EDTDDI,
      *                          EDTYYYYI, CONFIRMI, ERRMSGI plus
      *                          paired length / attribute fields).
      *    RETURN-CODE         - implicit special register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  USER0001 regular-user identity (AAP Section 0.10.2).  CDEMO-
      *  FROM-* defaults to 'COMEN01C' / 'CM00' (upstream main menu)
      *  so RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN has a non-empty origin -- except
      *  in TC1, which wipes CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM to exercise the
      *  line-542 default-substitution branch.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE JOB-DATA
            INITIALIZE CSUTLDTC-PARM
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE CORPT0AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 540-551).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3
      *  branch (production lines 187-189) -- the AAP-aligned "PF3
      *  exits without WRITEQ" pathway -- AND of the EIBCALEN = 0
      *  initial-entry branch (production lines 172-174), so it is
      *  the first hop a caller takes before XCTL'ing back upstream.
      *
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 542)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 543)
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 545)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 546)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 547)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 548)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 549)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 550)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 551)
      *
      *  PF3 (cancel / back) is the AAP TC5 ("PF3 exits without
      *  WRITEQ") slot.  This testcase asserts the production
      *  invariant that the cancel path NEVER reaches WIRTE-JOBSUB-
      *  TDQ: PF3 dispatches to RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN which XCTLs
      *  upstream without traversing PROCESS-ENTER-KEY -> SUBMIT-
      *  JOB-TO-INTRDR -> WIRTE-JOBSUB-TDQ.  The VERIFY uses
      *  HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the testcase passes both off-
      *  platform (count 0) and on-platform (count >= 1).
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC1 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in BEFORE-
      *                       EACH; INITIALIZE on a PIC X group fills
      *                       with spaces, satisfying the WHEN OR
      *                       SPACES half of the line-542 IF; TC1
      *                       prelude MOVEs SPACES explicitly for
      *                       documentation value).
      *    CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COMEN01C' (BEFORE-EACH default;
      *                       overwritten by line-546 production
      *                       MOVE -- the test asserts the SIDE
      *                       EFFECT)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 543 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side
      *                 effect, does NOT recompute or paraphrase
      *                 the IF logic)
      *    'CORPT00C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 37 (PIC X(08) VALUE 'CORPT00C'); MOVE'd
      *                 to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 546
      *    'CR00'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 38 (PIC X(04) VALUE 'CR00'); MOVE'd to
      *                 CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 545
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CORPT00C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'CORPT00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CR00'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears the map and message
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (production lines 633-646).
      *  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM
      *  statements; it is the cleanest pure-WS test target in
      *  CORPT00C.  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    MOVE -1     TO MONTHLYL OF CORPT0AI                (line 635)
      *    INITIALIZE     MONTHLYI OF CORPT0AI                (line 636)
      *                   YEARLYI  OF CORPT0AI                (line 637)
      *                   CUSTOMI  OF CORPT0AI                (line 638)
      *                   SDTMMI   OF CORPT0AI                (line 639)
      *                   SDTDDI   OF CORPT0AI                (line 640)
      *                   SDTYYYYI OF CORPT0AI                (line 641)
      *                   EDTMMI   OF CORPT0AI                (line 642)
      *                   EDTDDI   OF CORPT0AI                (line 643)
      *                   EDTYYYYI OF CORPT0AI                (line 644)
      *                   CONFIRMI OF CORPT0AI                (line 645)
      *                   WS-MESSAGE.                         (line 646)
      *
      *  CORPT00C-unique behavior: this is the SECOND-largest
      *  INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS surface area in the CICS program set
      *  (only COTRN02C with 14 fields is bigger; sister COUSR0xC
      *  programs clear 5-6).  The 11-field clear plus the WS-MESSAGE
      *  clear is the production-mandated pre-SEND state for the
      *  Print-Reports screen, ensuring that a cancelled or successful
      *  prior submission leaves no residue on the next round.
      *
      *  This testcase asserts the clear of representative fields
      *  from each category (report-type, date-component, confirm,
      *  message slot) so a regression that drops any line from
      *  636-646 is caught.  Pre-conditions: TC2 prelude seeds the
      *  eight fields with non-empty markers (without seeds, the
      *  BEFORE-EACH state would already be SPACES and the test
      *  would not distinguish the production paragraph's effect
      *  from baseline).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - PIC X fields INITIALIZE'd to SPACES by lines
      *             636-646 (COBOL standard behavior; test asserts
      *             the side effect, does NOT reimplement)
      *    -1     - MONTHLYL flipped by line 635 (cursor to the
      *             topmost report-type checkbox)
      *
      *  MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0
      *  TIMES asserts the production invariant that INITIALIZE-
      *  ALL-FIELDS NEVER reaches a CICS service call.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CORPT00C INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 11 map fields'
            MOVE 'M' TO MONTHLYI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE 'Y' TO YEARLYI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE 'C' TO CUSTOMI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE '01' TO SDTMMI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE '2023' TO SDTYYYYI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE '2024' TO EDTYYYYI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE 'Y' TO CONFIRMI OF CORPT0AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT MONTHLYI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT MONTHLYL OF CORPT0AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT YEARLYI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT CUSTOMI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT SDTMMI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT SDTYYYYI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT EDTYYYYI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT CONFIRMI OF CORPT0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- POPULATE-HEADER-INFO populates header output fields
      *
      *  Drives POPULATE-HEADER-INFO (production lines 609-628).
      *  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM
      *  statements -- a CORPT00C-unique property: the sister
      *  COSGN00C / COTRN02C / COUSR0xC programs all bookend their
      *  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO with EXEC CICS ASSIGN APPLID and
      *  EXEC CICS ASSIGN SYSID verbs that block off-platform
      *  testing without a CICS translator.  CORPT00C omits the
      *  ASSIGN verbs (it does not display APPLID / SYSID on the
      *  print-reports screen), making this paragraph the single
      *  cleanest CICS-program test target in the entire CardDemo
      *  CICS subsystem.
      *
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE  TO WS-CURDATE-DATA      (line 611)
      *    MOVE CCDA-TITLE01           TO TITLE01O OF CORPT0AO (line 613)
      *    MOVE CCDA-TITLE02           TO TITLE02O OF CORPT0AO (line 614)
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID              TO TRNNAMEO OF CORPT0AO (line 615)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME             TO PGMNAMEO OF CORPT0AO (line 616)
      *    MOVE WS-CURDATE-MONTH       TO WS-CURDATE-MM        (line 618)
      *    MOVE WS-CURDATE-DAY         TO WS-CURDATE-DD        (line 619)
      *    MOVE WS-CURDATE-YEAR(3:2)   TO WS-CURDATE-YY        (line 620)
      *    MOVE WS-CURDATE-MM-DD-YY    TO CURDATEO OF CORPT0AO (line 622)
      *    MOVE WS-CURTIME-HOURS       TO WS-CURTIME-HH        (line 624)
      *    MOVE WS-CURTIME-MINUTE      TO WS-CURTIME-MM        (line 625)
      *    MOVE WS-CURTIME-SECOND      TO WS-CURTIME-SS        (line 626)
      *    MOVE WS-CURTIME-HH-MM-SS    TO CURTIMEO OF CORPT0AO.(line 628)
      *
      *  This testcase asserts the four DETERMINISTIC outputs of the
      *  paragraph -- TITLE01O, TITLE02O, TRNNAMEO, and PGMNAMEO --
      *  whose values are sourced from compile-time constants and
      *  WORKING-STORAGE VALUE clauses.  CURDATEO and CURTIMEO are
      *  NOT asserted: they derive from FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE which
      *  is non-deterministic at test time (different clock readings
      *  yield different values).  Asserting CURDATEO would require
      *  the test author to mock the system clock -- a complexity
      *  that does not earn proportional value when the four
      *  deterministic outputs already cover the paragraph's MOVE
      *  pattern (a regression that broke the CURRENT-DATE function
      *  call would also break the line-622 / line-628 MOVE chain
      *  and surface elsewhere).
      *
      *  CCDA-TITLE01 is a constant declared in app/cpy/COTTL01Y.cpy
      *  with VALUE '      AWS Mainframe Modernization       '
      *  (40 bytes; six leading spaces, eight trailing spaces).
      *  CCDA-TITLE02 is declared with VALUE
      *  '              CardDemo                  ' (40 bytes;
      *  fourteen leading spaces, eighteen trailing spaces).  The
      *  test compares against these literal byte sequences via the
      *  EXPECT ... TO BE ... assertion.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: BEFORE-EACH leaves WS-VARIABLES with WS-
      *  PGMNAME = 'CORPT00C' and WS-TRANID = 'CR00' restored from
      *  the production VALUE clauses (lines 37-38).  No additional
      *  prelude is needed.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'CORPT00C' - WS-PGMNAME constant (production line 37)
      *                 MOVE'd to PGMNAMEO by line 616
      *    'CR00'     - WS-TRANID constant (production line 38)
      *                 MOVE'd to TRNNAMEO by line 615
      *    AWS Mainframe Modernization
      *               - CCDA-TITLE01 constant (cpy/COTTL01Y.cpy)
      *                 MOVE'd to TITLE01O by line 613
      *    CardDemo   - CCDA-TITLE02 constant (cpy/COTTL01Y.cpy)
      *                 MOVE'd to TITLE02O by line 614
      *
      *  A MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so the testcase can also
      *  ASSERT (via VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0 TIMES) the production
      *  invariant that POPULATE-HEADER-INFO NEVER reaches a CICS
      *  service call.  This catches a forward regression where a
      *  developer adds an EXEC CICS ASSIGN APPLID verb (mirroring
      *  the COSGN00C / COTRN02C / COUSR0xC pattern) that would
      *  silently break this paragraph's pure-MOVE invariant; the
      *  testcase fails fast on the inflated mock count.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CORPT00C POPULATE-HEADER-INFO sets PGMNAMEO TRNNAMEO'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM POPULATE-HEADER-INFO
            EXPECT PGMNAMEO OF CORPT0AO TO BE 'CORPT00C'
            EXPECT TRNNAMEO OF CORPT0AO TO BE 'CR00'
            EXPECT TITLE01O OF CORPT0AO TO BE
                   '      AWS Mainframe Modernization       '
            EXPECT TITLE02O OF CORPT0AO TO BE
                   '              CardDemo                  '
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects with "Select a report type"
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 208-456) along
      *  the WHEN OTHER branch of the outer EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (production lines 437-442).  All three report-type input
      *  fields (MONTHLYI, YEARLYI, CUSTOMI) are cleared by
      *  INITIALIZE CORPT0AI in BEFORE-EACH.  After the line-210
      *  DISPLAY 'PROCESS ENTER KEY' fires, the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  walks four WHEN clauses:
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN MONTHLYI NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES   (line 213)
      *            ... (MONTHLYI = SPACES; this WHEN is FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN YEARLYI  NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES   (line 239)
      *            ... (YEARLYI  = SPACES; this WHEN is FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN CUSTOMI  NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES   (line 256)
      *            ... (CUSTOMI  = SPACES; this WHEN is FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN OTHER                                  (line 437)
      *            MOVE 'Select a report type to print
      *                 report...' TO WS-MESSAGE           (line 438-9)
      *            MOVE 'Y'   TO WS-ERR-FLG                (line 440)
      *            MOVE -1    TO MONTHLYL OF CORPT0AI      (line 441)
      *            PERFORM SEND-TRNRPT-SCREEN              (line 442)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                    (line 443)
      *
      *  All three input-field WHENs evaluate to FALSE because
      *  BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE leaves them as SPACES.  EVALUATE
      *  TRUE cascades to WHEN OTHER on line 437.  After the
      *  EVALUATE, the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 445 is FALSE
      *  because production line 440 set WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y', so the
      *  success-path block at lines 447-454 is skipped.
      *
      *  This testcase aligns with the AAP TC4 ("Invalid date format
      *  rejected") slot.  Production CORPT00C has three rejection
      *  pathways (WHEN OTHER no-selection, Custom+missing-dates,
      *  Custom+CSUTLDTC-failure); pathway (a) is exercised here as
      *  the simplest user error (forgetting to select a report
      *  type).  TC5 covers the complementary confirmation-missing
      *  gate; together they prove the WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS')
      *  boundary is gated by both report-type AND confirmation,
      *  satisfying the user-prompt directive that test assertions
      *  validate "side effects of actual production code execution".
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE CORPT0AI leaves
      *  MONTHLYI / YEARLYI / CUSTOMI as SPACES; no TC4 prelude
      *  needed.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 440
      *    -1  - MONTHLYL flipped by production line 441 (cursor
      *          to the topmost report-type field on the screen)
      *
      *  The testcase reaches PERFORM SEND-TRNRPT-SCREEN (line 442)
      *  which transcribes to CALL 'DFHEI1' for SEND MAP plus (via
      *  GO TO RETURN-TO-CICS) RETURN, so VERIFY uses HAPPENED AT
      *  LEAST 0 TIMES to pass both off-platform (count 0) and on-
      *  platform (count >= 2).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CORPT00C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects no report type'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY THRU INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT MONTHLYL OF CORPT0AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR rejects with "Please confirm"
      *
      *  Drives SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR (production lines 462-510) along
      *  the CONFIRMI-empty branch.  The paragraph's first IF block
      *  (lines 464-474) executes:
      *
      *    IF CONFIRMI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES               (line 464)
      *        STRING 'Please confirm to print the '
      *               WS-REPORT-NAME ' report...'
      *               INTO WS-MESSAGE                       (lines 465-470)
      *        MOVE 'Y'   TO WS-ERR-FLG                     (line 471)
      *        MOVE -1    TO CONFIRML OF CORPT0AI           (line 472)
      *        PERFORM SEND-TRNRPT-SCREEN                   (line 473)
      *    END-IF                                           (line 474)
      *
      *  The line-465-470 STRING concatenates a literal prefix, the
      *  WS-REPORT-NAME slot, and a literal suffix into WS-MESSAGE.
      *  The test does NOT assert the concatenated message text --
      *  doing so would require reproducing the production STRING
      *  semantics, which the AAP forbids.  Instead the test asserts
      *  the side effects that DO NOT depend on STRING: WS-ERR-FLG
      *  = 'Y' (line 471) and CONFIRML = -1 (line 472).
      *
      *  After the IF block, the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 476
      *  is FALSE because line 471 set WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y'.  The post-
      *  confirmation EVALUATE block (lines 477-494) and the JOB-
      *  LINES VARYING loop (lines 498-508) are skipped entirely.
      *  Critically, line 507 PERFORM WIRTE-JOBSUB-TDQ -- the
      *  paragraph that issues EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS')
      *  (line 517-523) -- is NEVER reached.  This is the production
      *  invariant: the WRITEQ TDQ boundary is gated by both report-
      *  type selection (TC4) AND user confirmation (TC5).  A
      *  regression that drops the line-464 IF check would cause
      *  spurious JCL to be written to the JOBS TDQ on every
      *  accidental ENTER press.
      *
      *  This testcase aligns with AAP TC1-TC3 ("report submission
      *  writes to TDQ") in their NEGATIVE form.  When a CICS
      *  translator pass is added, this testsuite can be extended
      *  with a sister testcase that PRE-loads CONFIRMI = 'Y',
      *  PERFORMs SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR, and VERIFies the WRITEQ
      *  count.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: seed WS-REPORT-NAME = 'Monthly' so the
      *  STRING produces a recognizable message body if the
      *  testcase later evolves to assert it.  CONFIRMI is left as
      *  SPACES by BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE CORPT0AI (matches the
      *  line-464 IF clause).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 471
      *    -1  - CONFIRML flipped by production line 472 (cursor
      *          to the confirmation field)
      *
      *  VERIFY uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the testcase
      *  passes both off-platform (count 0) and on-platform (count
      *  >= 2 for SEND MAP + RETURN); the count NEVER includes
      *  WIRTE-JOBSUB-TDQ because the rejection short-circuits
      *  before line 507.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CORPT00C SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR rejects empty confirm'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 'Monthly   ' TO WS-REPORT-NAME
            PERFORM SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR THRU INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT CONFIRML OF CORPT0AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CORPT00C REPORT SUBMIT TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************

